docs/reviews/anchor-signatures/CODEX-REVIEW.md:67:   Correct conditional statement: an exact signature demonstrably existing before signing capability became available to the adversary cannot be manufactured afterward and substituted into that old receipt while the commitment and temporal evidence remain secure. Historical authenticity additionally requires the appropriate signing/key-use assumptions before that bound, authentic historical key authority, and no relevant pre-bound compromise. A later P-256 break need not invalidate such historical evidence by itself. It does not cure earlier theft, unauthorized pre-T signing, misissuance, or whole-author-sphere capture. It does not prove the issuer itself obtained the OTS stamp or uniquely issued the bundle.
    78	## A2.1 "Confirmed within δ": one predicate, both sides
    79	
